  "title": "Standing Klaw/OpenClaw lane — harden listener ownership, auth path, budget cap, and K3 identity before any hire",
  "description": "Bounded follow-up from JAC-3928.\n\nGoal:\nprepare the standing Klaw/OpenClaw path so it can be re-evaluated in a later gate, without treating it as live now.\n\nObserved gaps from Zatara gate review on 2026-08-01:\n- port 18679 listener ownership is ambiguous: one openclaw-gateway process is owned by /Applications/Kimi.app and one by launchd (ai.openclaw.gateway)\n- agent d216ee6e-caa8-4521-8452-3c546cf08143 still shows title \"Kimi K2 KimiClaw agent on Aegis\"\n- budgetMonthlyCents remains 0\n- status=error with Anthropic failover auth missing\n- secret_ref-backed credential hardening remains required but is not yet board-visible in the live read path\n\nRequested outcome:\n1. Reduce listener ownership on port 18679 to one expected supervisor/process.\n2. Remove the current failover auth error and document the deterministic provider/auth path.\n3. Update standing-agent identity from K2 to K3 only after the runtime actually matches that identity.\n4. Set a non-zero monthly budget cap appropriate for board review.\n5. Produce board-visible proof that standing credentials are secret-backed (no plaintext token/device key in control-plane config).\n6. Do not hire, route, or present this standing agent as",
